From: Oz64 WiFi bring-up <noreply@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] aic8800: disable BT-over-SDIO and BT/WiFi coexist

The AIC8800DC connected over SDIO on the Pine64 Oz64 (and the vendor
driver built here) hangs the SDIO bus shortly after the FullMAC interface
is created.  The failing command is TDLS_SDIO_BT_SEND_CFM (msg id 3089),
i.e. the BT-over-SDIO send path introduced by CONFIG_SDIO_BT, which runs
right after btsdio_init().  Once the bus is wedged, aicwf_sdio_hal_irqhandler
spins on reads returning -110/0xff and the system becomes unusable.

We do not use the SDIO Bluetooth on this board, so disable CONFIG_SDIO_BT
(and CONFIG_COEX) for both the bsp and fdrv modules.  With these off the
WiFi comes up, scans, associates and passes traffic.
--- a/extdrv/wireless/aic8800/aic8800_bsp/Makefile
+++ b/extdrv/wireless/aic8800/aic8800_bsp/Makefile
@@ -31,6 +31,6 @@
 CONFIG_RESV_MEM_SUPPORT ?= y
 CONFIG_AMSDU_RX = y
 CONFIG_IRQ_FALL ?= n
-CONFIG_SDIO_BT = y
+CONFIG_SDIO_BT = n
 CONFIG_RADAR_OR_IR_DETECT =n
 CONFIG_FOR_IPCAM = n
--- a/extdrv/wireless/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/Makefile
+++ b/extdrv/wireless/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/Makefile
@@ -72,11 +72,11 @@
 CONFIG_RADAR_OR_IR_DETECT =n
 CONFIG_DOWNLOAD_FW =n
 CONFIG_RFTEST=y
 CONFIG_USB_BT =n
-CONFIG_SDIO_BT=y
+CONFIG_SDIO_BT=n
 CONFIG_USE_5G ?= y
 CONFIG_CREATE_TRACE_POINTS = n
 CONFIG_TXRX_THREAD_PRIO = y
 # CONFIG_COEX = n for BT_ONLY, CONFIG_COEX =y for combo and sw
-CONFIG_COEX = y
+CONFIG_COEX = n
 CONFIG_RX_NETIF_RECV_SKB = y
